    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear focal point. With a score of 82.13, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** capitalizes on a prime matchup against Ober, benefiting from a soft 4.80 xERA and, crucially, a slow pitcher delivery that signals high efficiency for our pursuit of stolen bases. **Christian Yelich** and **Kazuma Okamoto** also project as high-end starters today; **Christian Yelich** leverages a strong platoon advantage to anchor the top of our order, while **Kazuma Okamoto** faces a favorable 4.67 xERA mark, allowing his elite base projection to translate into a solid 70.30 score. These three provide the heavy lifting required to keep us competitive in the scarcest 5x5 category while maintaining a strong floor for counting stats.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, with **Chase Meidroth** representing the most difficult omission. Despite his 36.69 score, **Chase Meidroth** was ultimately benched because his ninth-place spot in the order significantly depressed his run-scoring ceiling, keeping him below our 40.0 efficiency threshold. While **Yordan Alvarez** sits at a moderate 59.18 due to a tougher matchup against the 3.23 xERA of Kremer, his elite xwOBA of .475 keeps him in the starting lineup to chase home runs. Conversely, we continue to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim**, who remains sidelined in the minors, and we are managing our remaining depth\u2014including **Colt Keith**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Carson Benge**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez**\u2014strictly against our daily efficiency model to preserve our game caps. **Dillon Dingler**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Junior Caminero** round out the active roster, providing necessary coverage, though we are wary of the 2.85 xERA Miller faces against **Casey Schmitt**, which serves as the primary risk factor in today's projection.",
